{title: Joy to the World}
{artist: Isaac Watts / George Frideric Handel}
{genre: Christmas}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Carol}
{key: D}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 115장}
{title_ko: 기쁘다 구주 오셨네}
{score: joy-to-the-world.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Joy to the world, the [A]Lord is come
Let [D]earth re[G]ceive her [D]King
Let every [D]heart pre[G]pare Him [D]room
And heaven and [A]nature [D]sing
And heaven and [A]nature [D]sing
And heaven, and heaven and [D]nature [A]sing[D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Joy to the world, the [A]Saviour reigns
Let [D]men their [G]songs em[D]ploy
While fields and [D]floods, rocks, [G]hills and [D]plains
Repeat the sounding [A]joy
Repeat the sounding [A]joy
Repeat, repeat the sounding [D]joy[A][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]No more let sins and [A]sorrows grow
Nor [D]thorns in[G]fest the [D]ground
He comes to [D]make His [G]blessings [D]flow
Far as the curse is [A]found
Far as the curse is [A]found
Far as, far as the curse is [D]found[A][D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]He rules the world with [A]truth and grace
And [D]makes the [G]nations [D]prove
The glories of His [D]righteous[G]ness
And wonders of His [A]love
And wonders of His [A]love
And wonders, wonders of His [D]love[A][D]
{end_of_verse}
